-- src:290 | quan công an (nếu có).
-- "phụ thuộc vào yêu cầu của từng trường hợp cụ thể": the list is what Article 7 names for
-- the kind of case; which of them UIC asks for in a given case is left to UIC.
-- Each line is one row of the article's lists, in its order, as
-- `A listed document` OF document, gathered by UIC with the policyholder, only if there is one.
@ref UIC Rules, Part 1, Article 7 (src:243-290)
GIVEN c IS A `The kind of case for Article 7`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A listed document`
`Art 7 — the documents listed for` c MEANS
    concat (LIST `7.1.1 to 7.1.2.3`, `7.1.2.4`, `7.1.3 and 7.1.4`, `7.1.5`, `7.2.1`, `7.2.2`, `7.2.3`, `7.3`)
    WHERE
        `7.1.1 to 7.1.2.3` MEANS
            LIST (`A listed document` OF `notice of the loss and request for compensation`,                       FALSE, FALSE)
               , (`A listed document` OF `the insurance contract, or the parts of it UIC asks for`,               FALSE, FALSE)
               , (`A listed document` OF `the vehicle registration and the driver's valid licence`,               FALSE, FALSE)
               , (`A listed document` OF `papers on a sale, transfer, gift or authorisation to use the vehicle`,  FALSE, TRUE)
        `7.1.2.4` MEANS
            IF   c's `in temporary circulation or within first registration`
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE LIST (`A listed document` OF `the valid inspection certificate`,                                 FALSE, FALSE)
        `7.1.3 and 7.1.4` MEANS
            LIST (`A listed document` OF `the record of damage, quotes, invoices and receipts for repair or replacement`, FALSE, FALSE)
               , (`A listed document` OF `papers proving necessary and reasonable costs of limiting the loss or following UIC's instructions`, FALSE, FALSE)
               , (`A listed document` OF `the court's judgment or decision in force`,                             FALSE, TRUE)
        `7.1.5` MEANS
            IF   c's `involving a third party`
            THEN LIST (`A listed document` OF `papers to preserve or transfer the right to recover from the third party`, FALSE, FALSE)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `7.2.1` MEANS
            IF   c's `the police took part in settling the accident`
            THEN LIST (`A listed document` OF `the record of the scene examination`,                              TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the scene diagram and photographs`,                                TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the record of examination of the vehicles involved`,               TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the preliminary report of the initial investigation`,              TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the accident settlement record and the investigation conclusion, or equivalent`, TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the agreement or conciliation record`,                             TRUE, TRUE)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `7.2.2` MEANS
            IF   c's `involving a third party`
            THEN LIST (`A listed document` OF `documents on the third party's liability`,                         TRUE, FALSE)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `7.2.3` MEANS
            LIST (`A listed document` OF `the damage assessment record agreed by the parties`,                    TRUE, FALSE)
        `7.3` MEANS
            IF   c's `theft or robbery of the vehicle or a part`
            THEN LIST (`A listed document` OF `the theft or robbery report certified by the police`,              TRUE, FALSE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the decision to prosecute and investigate`,                        TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the decision to suspend the investigation or the prosecution`,     TRUE, TRUE)
                    , (`A listed document` OF `the declaration of loss of the vehicle's papers left in it, certified by the police`, TRUE, TRUE)
            ELSE EMPTY

§§§ `Article 8 — Double insurance`

-- The heading says Article 8 does not apply to Part 2.
